cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Memora: Reference Implementation of the Bitemporal
  Provenance Memory Architecture (BPMA)
message: >-
  If you use this software or the accompanying paper,
  please cite them as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Marko
    family-names: Vidrih
    email: marko@creatus.ai
    affiliation: Creatus.ai
repository-code: 'https://github.com/Nifty0x/memora'
abstract: >-
  Memora is the open-source reference implementation of the
  Bitemporal Provenance Memory Architecture (BPMA), an
  append-only, provenance-first memory substrate for AI
  agents. Every input is recorded as an immutable Memory
  Event carrying its principal (human, agent, or pipeline,
  with model version) and bitemporal coordinates. Facts
  extracted from those events (Claims) carry validity
  intervals and supersession links, so prior beliefs remain
  queryable. All recall structures are derived, versioned,
  replayable projections. The package also contains
  AuditEval, a benchmark of five provenance query classes.
keywords:
  - AI agents
  - agent memory
  - long-term memory
  - provenance
  - bitemporal
  - event sourcing
  - auditability
  - LLM agents
